    "created_at": "2020-06-01T09:30:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-01T09:30:28Z",
    "body": "As far as `unicode-bidi: isolate` consistently breaks up text run (that `<div style=\"display: inline\">` behaves the same way as `<span style=\"unicode-bidi: isolate\">`), that sounds acceptable.\r\n\r\nWhether kerning should be applied on text across `unicode-bidi: isolate` boundary value, I'm not exactly sure. It seems to me that Gecko always breaks text run when the bidi embedding level changes, which I think makes sense, because text with different bidi embedding level can potentially get reordered, and indeed `unicode-bidi: isolate` changes the level.\r\n\r\nMaybe ideally we should always apply kerning post bidi reorder, but that can be problematic as kerning affects layout...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
