    "created_at": "2020-06-01T09:44:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-01T09:44:42Z",
    "body": "ISTM that `unicode-bidi: isolate` is expressing a clear boundary, such that the content within the `isolate` element is independent of its context. So I wouldn't expect text shaping effects (such as kerning, but also contextual forms, ligatures, etc) that apply to runs of characters to get applied across that boundary.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
